# Qobuz API — Quick Reference

Qobuz exposes an **undocumented** private REST API at:

```
https://www.qobuz.com/api.json/0.2/
```

Unlike Deezer, there is **no anonymous access** — every endpoint requires an
`app_id` plus a `user_auth_token` from a real Qobuz account.

---

## Authentication

Three pieces are required:

1. **`app_id`** — application ID. Present in the web player JavaScript bundle.
2. **`app_secret`** — application secret, needed to sign protected endpoints
   (e.g. `track/getFileUrl`).
3. **`user_auth_token`** — obtained by logging into `user/login` with a Qobuz
   account (email + MD5'd password).

### Scraping app_id / app_secret from the web player

The login page references a bundle.js file. Fetch it and locate the
production credentials block:

```bash
curl -s https://play.qobuz.com/login | grep -o 'src="[^"]*bundle.js"'
curl -s <bundle_url_from_above> | grep -oE 'production:.*appSecret:"[^"]*"'
```

Extracted (2026-09, build 8.2.0-b034):

| Env        | app_id     | app_secret                       |
|------------|-----------|----------------------------------|
| production | `798273057` | `05a4851e74ee47fda346f50cfdfc4f09` |
| integration| `377257687` | `f686f063cb0841079d48495d4dea7cf2` |
| nightly    | `377257687` | `05a4851e74ee47fda346f50cfdfc4f09` |

Note: app_id = app_secret are a **matched pair**. Using a mismatched secret
against `track/getFileUrl` returns `400 Invalid Request Signature`.

### Logging in

```
POST /user/login
Headers:  X-App-Id: <app_id>
Params:   email=<email>&password=<md5(password)>&app_id=<app_id>
```

Response contains `user_auth_token`. Add it as a session header:

```
X-User-Auth-Token: <user_auth_token>
```

With both `X-App-Id` and `X-User-Auth-Token` headers set, search and metadata
endpoints work. Without them → `401 User authentication is required`.

---

## Search endpoints

All accept `query`, `limit`, `offset` (no signature needed, but require the
auth token):

| Endpoint          | Description                |
|-------------------|----------------------------|
| `catalog/search`  | Cross-catalog (all types)  |
| `track/search`    | Tracks only                |
| `album/search`    | Albums only                |
| `artist/search`   | Artists only               |
| `playlist/search` | Playlists only             |

Example (track search):

```bash
curl -s "https://www.qobuz.com/api.json/0.2/track/search" \
  -H "X-App-Id: 798273057" \
  -H "X-User-Auth-Token: <token>" \
  -G --data-urlencode "query=wyclef jean young thug" \
  --data-urlencode "limit=5"
```

Track result shape (JSON): track has `id`, `title`, `version`, `duration`,
`released_at`, `album{title,released_at,release_date_original,genre}`,
`performer{name}`, `media_type`, etc.

---

## Metadata endpoints

| Endpoint        | Params                          |
|-----------------|---------------------------------|
| `track/get`     | `track_id=<id>`                 |
| `album/get`     | `album_id=<id>`                 |
| `artist/get`    | `artist_id=<id>` (+ `extra=albums`) |
| `playlist/get`  | `playlist_id=<id>` (+ `extra=tracks`) |

These callers already carry the auth headers, so no signature is required.

---

## Signed endpoints

Some endpoints need an **MD5 request signature**:

`track/getFileUrl` (streaming URL):

```
sig = md5("trackgetFileUrlformat_id<fmt>intentstreamtrack_id<track_id>" + "<unix_ts>" + "<app_secret>")
params: request_ts=<unix_ts>&request_sig=<sig>&track_id=<id>&format_id=<fmt>&intent=stream
```

Quality IDs: `5`=MP3 320, `6`=FLAC 16-bit, `7`=FLAC 24-bit ≤96kHz, `27`=FLAC
24-bit >96kHz.

`favorite/getUserFavorites`:

```
sig = md5("favoritegetUserFavorites" + "<unix_ts>" + "<app_secret>")
```

---

## Current status (tested 2026-09-16)

- `app_id` / `app_secret` were successfully scraped from the live bundle.js.
- **Blocked:** search + metadata return `401 User authentication is required`
  because a `user_auth_token` could not be obtained without Qobuz account
  credentials (email/password).
- Guest/device login attempts and legacy app IDs (`950244987`, `2146024384`,
  `916443999`, `355768545`) are all rejected with `400`/`401`.

**Conclusion:** to run the "wyclef jean / young thug" metadata lookup, a real
Qobuz account password is required to mint a `user_auth_token`.